From 9eb2bc038da58344b3870283716123dd46cf2f49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:04:40 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] corner: Fixes the swapped bottom corners; permits actions
 with an argument.

Entering the bottom-left corner ran the BottomRightEnter action, and the
bottom-right corner the BottomLeftEnter one (same for 'Leave'): eg. with the
example configuration's 'BottomLeftEnter = LockScreen', the screen locked in
the bottom-right corner. The action of a corner is now looked up in one
place, _wlmaker_corner_action(), for entering and leaving, and tested.

A hot corner could also only trigger an action without argument, so it
could not launch a program, as Window Maker's hot corners do
(HotCornerActions). Corner actions now also accept the array format of
KeyBindings; the plain format is unchanged:

    TopLeftEnter = (ShellExecute, "rofi -show drun");
    BottomLeftEnter = LockScreen;

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/corner.c | 267 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 207 insertions(+), 60 deletions(-)

